# NEWS FEATURE — COMPLETE IMPLEMENTATION DOCUMENTATION

**Project:** `car_sales`\
**Flutter package:** `car_sales_app` (folder `mobile_app`)\
**Feature root:** `lib/features/bottom/news/`\
**Framework:** Flutter and Dart (SDK `^3.12.2`, Flutter 3.44.8)\
**Platform:** Android\
**Market:** Ethiopia\
**Scope:** The News tab (News & Reviews + Images & Videos sub-tabs), article search, article detail screen, video player screen, image gallery, and favourites integration\
**Purpose:** Act as the single source of truth for the News feature. Inspect, repair, extend and verify the existing implementation without rebuilding working code.

---

# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

The News feature provides a complete content feed for automotive news, expert reviews, videos, and image galleries. It must deliver:

1. A tabbed main page with "News & Reviews" and "Images & Videos" sections.
2. Horizontal filter pills (All / Reviews / Special Reports) to filter articles.
3. Horizontally scrollable article cards with category badges, favourite buttons, and tap-to-open.
4. A horizontally scrollable video carousel with play overlay and view/like counts.
5. Image collections (vehicle photo sets) with 360° view indicators.
6. Article and video detail screens with full body text, author info, and share/bookmark actions.
7. Search across all content (articles, videos, collections).
8. Favourites integration via a shared `FavoritesStore`.

## 1.1 Core rules

1. Inspect the existing project before editing anything.
2. Preserve correct and useful code. The article card, video card, and collection card widgets are well designed and should be kept.
3. Repair broken code.
4. Update incomplete components.
5. Remove genuinely redundant code only after verifying it is safe to remove.
6. Reuse existing models, assets, navigation, state management and services.
7. Never duplicate the `NewsArticle` or `NewsVideo` models, or the `MockNewsRepository`.
8. Preserve New Cars, Used Cars, Compare and Alerts functionality.
9. Use Ethiopian-market content and ETB pricing.
10. Do not claim an integration works unless it has been verified on a device or emulator.
11. The News feature is frontend-only. All data lives in `MockNewsRepository`; when a backend arrives, only the `fetch*` methods need swapping — the UI does not change (see the repo comment in `mock_news_repository.dart`).

# 2. FEATURE SCOPE AND NON-GOALS

## 2.1 In scope

- `NewsScreen` (tab page, lib/features/bottom/news/news.dart).
- Main tabs: "News & Reviews" and "Images & Videos".
- Sub-tabs within each: 'All / Reviews / Special Reports' for articles; 'Images' and 'Videos' for media.
- Filter pills: All / Reviews / Special Reports.
- Article cards (`_ArticleCard`) with cover image, category badge, title, author, time ago, view count, and favourite toggle.
- Video cards (`_VideoCard`) with 16:9 thumbnail, play button, category badge, title, author, time ago, view count, like count.
- Collection cards (`_CollectionCard`) with cover image, 360° badge, image count badge, and vehicle name.
- Article detail screen (`ArticleDetailScreen`).
- Video detail screen (`VideoDetailsScreen`).
- Image gallery screen (`ImageGalleryScreen`).
- News search screen (`NewsSearchScreen`).
- Favourite integration via `FavoritesStore.instance`.
- `categoryColorOf()` mapping and `NewsArticle.searchMatches()`.
- `MockNewsRepository` with `fetchArticles()`, `fetchVideos()`, `fetchCollections()`.

## 2.2 Out of scope (do not build in this feature)

- A real backend or API. All data lives in `MockNewsRepository`; the comment in that file explicitly says "frontend only".
- A persisted favourites store across app restarts. `FavoritesStore` is in-memory only (documented in section 22).
- Live video playback. The video screen shows metadata only; actual video URLs are not part of the model.
- Push notifications. Alerts notifications are a separate feature (see `docs/alert.doc`).
- A second news database or duplicate content models.
- Indian rupee prices or lakh notation. All prices in the mock data are in ETB.
- Auto-playing videos. Video thumbnails are static images.

