## 3.1 Shared code rules

- `PageTopBar`, `NewsSkeletonCards`, `NewsEmptyState` are shared widgets. Do not copy them.
- `AppIcons.news`, `AppIcons.favorite`, `AppIcons.favoriteBorder`, `AppIcons.search`, `AppIcons.notification` are the only icon needs.
- `MockNewsRepository` is the single data source. Do not create a second repository.
- `FavoritesStore.instance` is the single favourite tracker. Both `ArticleDetailScreen` and `_ArticleCard` use it.
- All colour tokens come from `AppColors`. Do not hardcode hex values.
- All dimension tokens come from `AppDimens`. Do not use raw numbers.

# 4. SCREEN FLOW AND NAVIGATION MAP

```
Bottom navigation (index 3, "News")
        |
        v
NewsScreen  (lib/features/bottom/news/news.dart)
  |
  |--- main tabs: "News & Reviews" (default) / "Images & Videos"
  |    |
  |    |--- "News & Reviews" ----------> _buildNewsList()
  |    |    |--- filter pills: All / Reviews / Special Reports
  |    |    |--- list of _ArticleCard widgets (paginated via ListenableBuilder + FavoritesStore)
  |    |    |--- empty state: NewsEmptyState()
  |    |    |--- loading: NewsSkeletonCards()
  |    |
  |    |--- tap article -------------> ArticleDetailScreen(article)
  |    |    |--- header: article title + author
  |    |    |--- body: article.body paragraphs
  |    |    |--- bottom: share button + favourite toggle
  |    |    |--- favourite toggles FavoritesStore.instance
  |    |
  |    |--- sub-tab "Images & Videos" ---> _buildMediaList()
  |         |--- sub-tabs: "Images" / "Videos"
  |         |--- if "Images": list of _CollectionCard -> ImageGalleryScreen(collection)
  |         |--- if "Videos": list of _VideoCard -> VideoDetailsScreen(video)
  |
  |--- tap favourites icon ---------> FavoritesStore.toggle(id) + SnackBar
  |--- tap search icon -------------> NewsSearchScreen (pushes named route)
```

Rules:

- Tab switching must not push routes. The `NewsScreen` rebuilds its body when the main or sub-tab changes.
- Sub-screens are pushed with `MaterialPageRoute` and popped with `Navigator.pop`.
- `ArticleDetailScreen` and `VideoDetailsScreen` each receive a model object; they never navigate back with arguments.
- Favourite state lives in `FavoritesStore.instance`; toggling it shows a 1-second snackbar ("Saved to favourites" / "Removed from favourites").
- The search screen returns to `NewsScreen` when the user pops it.

# 5. COMPLETE PAGE STRUCTURE

The News tab is a single vertical scroll (ListView inside a ColoredBox) with these blocks in this exact order:

1. Header (`_buildHeader()`) — `PageTopBar` with title "News", trailing search icon and favourites icon.
2. Main tab selector: horizontal underline tabs "News & Reviews" / "Images & Videos".
3. If "News & Reviews":
   a. Filter pills row: All / Reviews / Special Reports.
   b. Article list (ListView.builder) with `_ArticleCard` widgets.
   c. Empty state if no articles match the current filter.
   d. Skeleton cards while data loads.
4. If "Images & Videos":
   a. Sub-tab selector: "Images" / "Videos".
   b. If "Images": collection list (`_CollectionCard`) → `ImageGalleryScreen`.
   c. If "Videos": video list (`_VideoCard`) → `VideoDetailsScreen`.
   d. Empty state if no collections/videos.
   e. Skeleton cards while data loads.

Do not split these blocks into separate screens. The page is one scrollable surface inside the bottom tab.

