## 6.3 Spacing and radii

Use `AppDimens` only.

- Spacing: `xs 4`, `sm 8`, `md 12`, `lg 16`, `xl 24`, `xxl 32`.
- Radii: `radiusSm 8`, `radiusMd 12`, `radiusLg 20`.
- Page list padding: `EdgeInsets.only(top: AppDimens.md)` for article list.
- Card padding: `EdgeInsets.fromLTRB(AppDimens.lg, AppDimens.sm, AppDimens.lg, AppDimens.sm)` for article/video/collection cards.
- Header padding: `EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: AppDimens.lg)` inside filter pills and collection cards.
- Skeleton block height: 96 for articles, 96 for videos, 96 for collections (see `NewsSkeletonCards`).
- Empty state illustration height: 172 (circular card).
- Tooltip/containers: width 42, height 42 for header action chips, `radiusMd 12`.

## 6.4 Icons and images

- Icons come from `AppIcons` (`lucide_icons_flutter`). Do not mix raw Material icons into the shared icon set.
- Car images load from `assets/images/` via `Image.asset` with error fallback to `image_not_supported_outlined`.
- All article/video/collection images use `BoxFit.cover` and must never be stretched.
- The catalogue file name convention is `'<Model>.jpg'`, for example `BMW 7 Series.jpg` (same convention as the Compare feature).
- Colours for category badges come from `categoryColorOf()` (see section 18.1). These are deterministic per category string.
- Favourite icons: `AppIcons.favorite` (filled, teal/red) when saved, `AppIcons.favoriteBorder` (outline, secondary) when not. Both are 20px.

# 7. TOP BAR AND HEADER ACTIONS

The News tab header uses `PageTopBar`:

```dart
PageTopBar(
  title: 'News',
  trailing: [
    _HeaderAction(
      icon: AppIcons.search,
      tooltip: 'Search',
      onTap: _openSearch,
    ),
    const SizedBox(width: AppDimens.sm),
    _HeaderAction(
      icon: AppIcons.favoriteBorder,
      tooltip: 'Favourites',
      onTap: () =>
          Navigator.of(context).pushNamed(AppRoutes.favourites),
    ),
  ],
)
```

- `PageTopBar` is a shared widget (`lib/shared/widgets/page_top_bar.dart`). It renders a `Container` with surface fill, a 1px divider bottom, and a `Column` with the title and a `Row` of trailing widgets.
- `_HeaderAction` is a 42x42 rounded square with surface fill, 1px divider border, 21px icon in textSecondary, wrapped in a `Tooltip`. Tapping opens the named route.
- Search pushes `AppRoutes.newsSearch` (`/news-search` → `NewsSearchScreen`).
- Favourites pushes the named route `AppRoutes.favourites` (currently a placeholder).

# 8. ARTICLE CARD

`_ArticleCard` is the core browsing widget for the "News & Reviews" section.

## 8.1 Structure

- Full-width container, `radiusLg`, surface fill, 1px `divider` border.
- `Column` with three child stacks + text column.
- **Cover image** (AspectRatio 16:9, `BoxFit.cover`, error fallback icon).
- **Category badge** (top-left): pill with category name, white text on category colour.
- **Favourite button** (top-right): circle with `AppIcons.favorite` (teal/red) or `AppIcons.favoriteBorder` (secondary). Toggling calls `FavoritesStore.toggle(id)` + snackbar.
- **Text column** (padding AppDimens.md):
  - Category in upper case (`category.toUpperCase()`), `labelSmall`, letterSpacing 1.1, category colour.
  - Title (`title`), `titleMedium`, max 3 lines, ellipsis, height 1.3, primary colour.
  - Metadata row: "By <author>" + "•" + "<timeAgo>", `bodySmall`, secondary colour.
  - View count row: `<n> views`, `bodySmall`, secondary colour, with visibility icon.

## 8.2 Interaction

- Whole card is `InkWell`; tapping calls `_openArticle(article)` → `ArticleDetailScreen`.
- Favourite button toggles `FavoritesStore.instance` and shows a 1-second snackbar.
- The snackbar content: `saved ? 'Removed from favourites' : 'Saved to favourites'`.

# 9. VIDEO CARD

`_VideoCard` is the browsing widget for the "Videos" sub-tab.

## 9.1 Structure

- Full-width container, `radiusLg`, surface fill, 1px `divider` border.
- `Column` with video cover + text column.
- **Cover image** (AspectRatio 16:9, `BoxFit.cover`, error fallback). Overlaid:
  - Large play button icon (`Icons.play_arrow`, size 38, white, on black38 circle).
  - Category badge (top-left): same pill style as article.
  - Duration badge (top-right): small rect with black54 background, white text, e.g., "8:12".
- **Text column** (padding AppDimens.md):
  - Category in upper case, `labelSmall`, letterSpacing 1.1, category colour.
  - Title (`title`), `titleMedium`, max 2 lines, ellipsis, height 1.3, primary colour.
  - Metadata row: "By <author>" + "•" + "<timeAgo>", `bodySmall`, secondary colour.
  - Views + likes row: "<n> views  <n> likes", `bodySmall`, secondary colour, with favourite-border icon.

## 9.2 Interaction

- Whole card is `InkWell`; tapping calls `_openVideo(video)` → `VideoDetailsScreen`.
- No favourite toggle on the video card itself (the detail screen has its own favourite logic).

# 10. COLLECTION CARD

`_CollectionCard` is the browsing widget for the "Images" sub-tab.

## 10.1 Structure

- Full-width container, `radiusLg`, surface fill, 1px `divider` border.
- `Column` with cover image + name + optional badges.
- **Cover image** (AspectRatio 16:9, `BoxFit.cover`, error fallback). Overlaid:
  - If `has360`: 360° badge (black54 pill, white "360° View" text, top-right).
  - Image count badge (bottom-left): black54 pill, white "<n> images" text.
- **Name** (bottom, `titleMedium`, primary colour, max 1 line, ellipsis).

## 10.2 Interaction

- Whole card is `InkWell`; tapping calls `_openGallery(collection)` → `ImageGalleryScreen`.
- No favourite toggle on the collection card.

# 11. IMAGE GALLERY SCREEN

`ImageGalleryScreen(collection:)` — reached from `_CollectionCard`.

- Scaffold with `AppColors.background`.
- App bar title: collection name, back arrow.
- Body: `GridView.count` or `PageView` of the collection's `galleryAssets` (the model lists asset file names).
- Each grid cell: `AspectRatio(16/9, child: Image.asset(...))` with `BoxFit.cover` and error fallback.
- No vertical scrolling inside the grid; the grid itself is the scrollable area.
- No favourite or share actions (the collection is a static image set).

# 12. ARTICLE DETAIL SCREEN

`ArticleDetailScreen(article:)` — reached from `_ArticleCard`.

## 12.1 App bar

- Title: article.title (`titleMedium`).
- Leading: back arrow.
- Actions: none currently (share button documented as a future P2 item).

## 12.2 Body

- `PageView` or single-scrolling `ListView` with the article body.
- Header row: article title large + author block.
- Body paragraphs: `body` is a `List<String>`; each paragraph rendered as `bodyMedium` with line height 1.55, primary colour.
- At the very bottom: a line showing `priceTag` if present (e.g., "From ETB 3,850,000"), in `labelLarge`, teal.
- No favourite toggle on this screen (the favourite action was on the card; the screen could add one later as P2).

## 12.3 Interaction

- Scrollable text only.
- No navigation out of the screen except the back arrow.

# 13. VIDEO DETAILS SCREEN

`VideoDetailsScreen(video:)` — reached from `_VideoCard`.

- Scaffold with `AppColors.background`.
- App bar title: video.title, back arrow.
- Body: similar structure to article detail but for video metadata:
  - Video title large.
  - Author block.
  - Description text.
  - Views + likes row.
  - Duration badge.
  - Keywords or tags if needed.
- No video playback URL; the model only stores metadata (title, author, timeAgo, views, likes, duration, keywords, description).

# 14. NEWS SEARCH SCREEN

`NewsSearchScreen` — pushed from the top-bar search icon.

- Scaffold with `AppColors.background`.
- App bar: title "Search News", back arrow.
- Body: `TextField` with hint "Search articles, videos, collections".
- As the user types, filter all three data sets via `MockNewsRepository.searchArticles`, `searchVideos`, `searchCollections`.
- Results displayed as a list (or Wrap of chips) of matching items from all three categories.
- Tapping a result navigates to the appropriate detail screen (ArticleDetailScreen / VideoDetailsScreen) or opens the gallery.

# 15. FAVOURITES STORE

`FavoritesStore.instance` — in-memory session-scoped favourite tracker.

```dart
class FavoritesStore extends ChangeNotifier {
  static final FavoritesStore instance = FavoritesStore._();
  final Set<String> _faved = {};
  bool get isFavorite(String id) => _faved.contains(id);
  void toggle(String id) {
    if (!_faved.remove(id)) _faved.add(id);
    notifyListeners();
  }
}
```

Rules:

- Toggling a favourite shows a 1-second snackbar ("Saved to favourites" / "Removed from favourites").
- The store is session-scoped: favourites are lost when the app restarts. This is a documented limitation (see section 22).
- Both `_ArticleCard` and `ArticleDetailScreen` use `FavoritesStore.instance.isFavorite(article.id)` to decide which icon to show.
- The `NewsScreen` rebuilds when `FavoritesStore.instance` changes (via `ListenableBuilder`).

# 15. DATA LAYER

## 14.1 The `NewsArticle` model

```dart
class NewsArticle {
  const NewsArticle({
    required this.id,
    required this.category,
    required this.title,
    required this.imageAsset,
    required this.author,
    required this.timeAgo,
    required this.views,
    required this.body,
    this.publishedDate = '',
    this.priceTag,
    this.keywords = const [],
  });

  final String id;
  final String category;
  final String title;
  final String imageAsset;
  final String author;
  final String timeAgo;
  final int views;
  final List<String> body; // paragraphs
  final String publishedDate;
  final String? priceTag;
  final List<String> keywords;

  Color get categoryColor => categoryColorOf(category);

  bool searchMatches(String query) {
    final q = query.trim().toLowerCase();
    if (q.isEmpty) return false;
    return title.toLowerCase().contains(q) ||
        category.toLowerCase().contains(q) ||
        keywords.any((k) => k.toLowerCase().contains(q));
  }
}
```

## 14.2 The `NewsVideo` model

```dart
class NewsVideo {
  const NewsVideo({
    required this.id,
    required this.title,
    required this.imageAsset,
    required this.category,
    required this.author,
    required this.timeAgo,
    required this.views,
    required this.likes,
    required this.duration,
    required this.keywords,
    required this.description,
  });

  final String id;
  final String title;
  final String imageAsset;
  final String category;
  final String author;
  final String timeAgo;
  final int views;
  final int likes;
  final String duration; // e.g. "8:12"
  final List<String> keywords;
  final String description;
}
```

## 14.3 The `VehicleImageCollection` model

```dart
class VehicleImageCollection {
  const VehicleImageCollection({
    required this.id,
    required this.name,
    required this.coverAsset,
    required this.has360,
    required this.keywords,
    required this.galleryAssets,
  });

  final String id;
  final String name;
  final String coverAsset;
  final bool has360;
  final List<String> keywords;
  final List<String> galleryAssets; // asset file names
}
```

## 14.4 `MockNewsRepository`

- `fetchArticles()` → returns the static `articles` list after a 500ms delay.
- `fetchVideos()` → returns the static `videos` list after a 500ms delay.
- `fetchCollections()` → returns the static `collections` list after a 500ms delay.
- Search helpers: `searchArticles(query)`, `searchVideos(query)`, `searchCollections(query)`.
- The delay is intentional: it exercises the loading states (skeleton cards). Do not remove it without also removing the skeleton UI.

## 14.5 Category colours

`categoryColorOf(category)` maps each of the 11 supported categories to a deterministic colour:

| Category | Colour |
| -------- | ------ |
| News | `AppColors.primary` (#1B5E20) |
| Reviews | `AppColors.accent` |
| Road Test | `AppColors.teal` (#0F8F83) |
| Features | `Color(0xFF5E35B1)` |
| Special Reports | `AppColors.red` |
| EV News | `AppColors.success` |
| New Cars | `AppColors.primaryLight` |
| Used Cars | `Color(0xFF6D4C41)` |
| Car Prices | `Color(0xFFF57F17)` |
| Maintenance | `Color(0xFF546E7A)` |
| Buying Guide | `Color(0xFF7B1FA2)` |

These colours are used for the category badge background and text. If a new category is added, extend the switch statement.

# 15. STATE MANAGEMENT AND CACHING

- No third-party state package. The feature uses `StatefulWidget` local state (`NewsScreen`) plus `ChangeNotifier` for `FavoritesStore`.
- `NewsScreen` holds `_mainTab`, `_mediaSubTab`, `_filter`, `_loading`, `_articles`, `_videos`, `_collections`.
- Data loading is triggered in `initState()` via `_loadData()`, which fetches all three futures in parallel.
- The 500ms simulated delay in `MockNewsRepository` means the UI always shows `NewsSkeletonCards()` initially.
- After data loads, `_loading = false` and the appropriate list is shown.
- `FavoritesStore.instance` is the only shared state; it is a `ChangeNotifier` so `ListenableBuilder` can react.
- Tab switches cause `setState` only, no widget rebuilding beyond the body column.

# 16. ROUTES AND NAVIGATION

| Route constant | Path | Target |
| --------------- | ---- | ------ |
| `AppRoutes.news` | `/news` | `NewsScreen` (registered in `AppRouter.routes()`) |
| `AppRoutes.newsSearch` | `/news-search` | `NewsSearchScreen` |
| `AppRoutes.favourites` | `/favourites` | `PlaceholderScreen` (stub, not yet a real feature) |

- Bottom navigation order: New, Used, Compare, News, Alerts. News is index 3 and uses `AppIcons.news` (`LucideIcons.newspaper`).
- The selected bottom navigation item is `AppColors.primary` (`#1B5E20`); unselected items are `Colors.grey[700]`.
- Sub-tab switching inside NewsScreen does not push routes; the body rebuilds.

# 17. LOADING, EMPTY AND ERROR STATES

Every asynchronous block in this feature has all three states.

| Location | Loading | Error | Empty |
| -------- | ------- | ----- | ----- |
| Article list | `NewsSkeletonCards()` (3 vertical skeleton cards) | `_InlineNotice`-style notice not yet implemented | `NewsEmptyState()` — centre illustration + "No articles available" |
| Video list | `NewsSkeletonCards()` | Same as above | `NewsEmptyState()` |
| Collection list | `NewsSkeletonCards()` | Same as above | `NewsEmptyState()` |
| All screens during initial load | `NewsSkeletonCards()` covers the whole column | n/a | n/a |

Rules:

- `NewsSkeletonCards()` is a static widget that shows three vertical skeleton blocks (height 96 each). It never animates, which keeps widget tests deterministic.
- The error state for article/video/collection lists is not yet implemented (a P2 item). For now, the empty state is shown when the filtered list is empty.
- `NewsEmptyState()` shows an automotive-themed illustration (bell + small car) with "All Caught Up" / "You have seen all notifications" text. The illustration is 172px circular card with `Color(0xFFE9F1FB)` fill.

# 18. KNOWN ISSUES AND DEFECTS

`flutter analyze` currently reports errors across the project. **News-specific issues** (verified against the code):

## 18.1 P0 — the feature does not compile

| ID | File | Problem | Required fix |
| -- | ---- | ------- | ------------ |
| P0-1 | `lib/core/constants/app_icons.dart` | `AppIcons.favorite`, `AppIcons.favoriteBorder`, `AppIcons.news`, `AppIcons.notification` are used but some may not exist as `static const IconData` | Verify the icon constants against `lucide_icons_flutter` 4.0.1; add missing ones using valid Lucide names (e.g., `bookmark` → `bookBookmark` or add the missing getter) |
| P0-2 | `lib/features/bottom/news/news.dart` (line 516) | `AppIcons.favorite` / `AppIcons.favoriteBorder` used inside `const` context but fields are not `const` | Change `AppIcons` fields from `static IconData` to `static const IconData` (see P0-4 below) |
| P0-3 | `lib/features/bottom/news/news.dart` | The `_HeaderAction` and `_UnderlineTab` widgets are not `const` where they could be, causing unnecessary rebuilds | Not a blocker, but clean up for performance |
| P0-4 | `lib/core/constants/app_icons.dart` | Icon fields are `static IconData` instead of `static const IconData`, causing every `const Icon(AppIcons....)` to fail with `const_with_non_constant_argument` | Change all icon fields to `static const IconData` (one fix fixes all features) |

## 18.2 P1 — correctness and data integrity

| ID | Location | Problem | Required fix |
| -- | -------- | ------- | ------------ |
| P1-1 | `news.dart`, `_buildNewsList()` | `ListenableBuilder(listenable: FavoritesStore.instance, ...)` causes the entire article list to rebuild whenever *any* favourite toggles, even articles not in view | Extract the favourite-check into the `_ArticleCard` only (it already does this); remove the `ListenableBuilder` wrapper from the list level — this was a redundant pattern |
| P1-2 | `mock_news_repository.dart` | The `articles` list has 24 entries but the `videos` list has only 5, and `collections` has 5. The UI assumes at least one item in each list but the empty states are not consistently wired | Ensure `NewsEmptyState()` is shown when `_filteredArticles.isEmpty`, `_videos.isEmpty`, or `_collections.isEmpty` |
| P1-3 | `news_search_screen.dart` | Search results navigate to the correct detail screens but do not pass the query; the search screen always opens the first article | Pass the search query or the selected article/video/collection through the navigator, so the detail screen can pre-filter or highlight matches |
| P1-4 | `news.dart` | The `_UnderlineTab` selected colour uses `AppColors.primary` but the colour token is `#1B5E20` (dark green). The visual contrast against the white surface may be low on some devices. Consider using `AppColors.teal` (`#0F8F83`) for better contrast, or document the intent | |
| P1-5 | `news.dart` | The filter pill selected text uses `Colors.white` on `AppColors.primary` (`#1B5E20`). The contrast ratio is adequate per WCAG AA, but the unselected pill uses `AppColors.textSecondary` (`#6B6B6B`) on `AppColors.surface` (`#FAFAFA`), which is fine. No change needed, but document the rationale | |

## 18.3 P2 — cleanup and future work

| ID | Location | Problem | Action |
| -- | -------- | ------- | ------ |
| P2-1 | `news.dart`, `_buildNewsList()` | `ListenableBuilder(listenable: FavoritesStore.instance, ...)` around the entire ListView is unnecessary and causes over-rebuilds | Remove the `ListenableBuilder`; the favourite state is already handled inside `_ArticleCard` |
| P2-2 | `news_search_screen.dart` | Search does not persist the query or highlight matches in the detail screen | Add query passing through the navigator; document as a future enhancement |
| P2-3 | `mock_news_repository.dart` | No "Load More" pagination; all articles are loaded at once. For a real backend, add cursor-based or offset-based pagination | Document the limitation; the UI does not need to change when the backend arrives |
| P2-4 | `news.dart` | The "Images & Videos" sub-tabs have no data fetching of their own; both sub-tabs just display the same `_loadData()` results filtered differently | The current `initState` fetches everything once; this is fine for the mock but would need refactoring for a real API with separate endpoints |
| P2-5 | `news.dart` | The `_UnderlineTab` animateContainer duration is 250ms but the tab change animation in the `PageView` shell may not sync | Ensure the underline animation syncs with the page swipe; consider using the same `PageController` if the shell provides one |
| P2-6 | `news.dart` | The favourite toggle in `_ArticleCard` shows a snackbar, but the `ListenableBuilder` at the list level also calls `notifyListeners()` via `FavoritesStore.instance`. The snackbar may fire twice if the user taps rapidly | Debounce the snackbar or show it only from the card level (already the case — the list `ListenableBuilder` should be removed per P2-1) |
| P2-7 | `news_search_screen.dart` | The search screen has no clear button on the text field when typing; users must manually delete text | Add a suffix `IconButton(icon: Icon(Icons.clear), onPressed: _controller.clear)` when the query is not empty |
| P2-8 | `news.dart` | The category filter pill for "Special Reports" uses the same colour as "Reviews" in some edge cases; verify the colour mapping is correct per the switch statement | The colour mapping is correct; this is a visual-QA item, not a code bug |

