`new_impl.dart` (56), `compare_catalogue.dart` (7), `select_car.dart` (7), `compare.dart` (5), `used.dart` (4), `search.dart` (3), `bottom_nav_bar.dart` (3), `article_detail_screen.dart` (4), `video_details_screen.dart` (2), `saved_reviews_screen.dart` (2), `compare_details.dart` (2) and many others also fail to compile. Fix them separately and report them separately. The News feature must not be blamed for them, and News work must not silently rewrite them.

# 19. EXISTING CODE REVIEW AND SAFE MODIFICATION

The News feature is largely written and the structure is good. Do not assume the code is wrong — inspect it first.

For each component:

- **Correct and useful:** keep it. The article card, video card, collection card, skeleton cards, empty state, and category colour mapping all follow the intended design.
- **Mostly correct:** update only what is needed. The filter pills and tab switching are fine.
- **Broken:** repair it. The missing `AppIcons` constants and the `const` field issue are broken.
- **Incomplete:** extend it. The `ListenableBuilder` over-rebuild, the search screen lacking query passing, and the error-state wiring are incomplete.
- **Duplicated:** keep the best implementation and remove the rest once it is safe. `SkeletonBlock` is used in three places already; the `ListenableBuilder` pattern is duplicated.
- **Unused:** remove only after confirming it is unnecessary.
- **Unclear:** investigate before changing or deleting it.

Before each implementation task:

1. Inspect the relevant files and dependencies.
2. Identify what must be preserved, fixed, updated or removed.
3. Report the intended file changes.
4. Make focused changes.
5. Verify with `flutter analyze` and `flutter test`.

Rules:

- Do not delete whole files or rebuild the feature from scratch.
- Do not create a second news repository or a second data model.
- Do not add a state-management package, a networking package or a database for this feature without an explicit decision.
- Keep every unrelated feature working: New Cars, Used Cars, Compare and Alerts.
- Keep prices in ETB and content relevant to the Ethiopian market.
- Distinguish pre-existing errors from new errors in the report.

# 20. INCREMENTAL IMPLEMENTATION PLAN

Implement and verify the feature in this order. Do not attempt every stage in one operation.

1. **Stage 1 — make it compile.** Add the missing `AppIcons` constants and make the icon fields `static const IconData`. Fix the `ListenableBuilder` over-rebuild in `_buildNewsList()`. Re-run `flutter analyze` and confirm the News errors are gone.
2. **Stage 2 — fix the favourite rebuild.** Remove the `ListenableBuilder(listenable: FavoritesStore.instance, ...)` wrapper from `_buildNewsList()` and verify the favourite toggle still works correctly from the card level only.
3. **Stage 3 — wire the search screen.** Add query passing through the navigator from `NewsSearchScreen` to the destination detail screen, and add a clear button to the text field.
4. **Stage 4 — harden the empty states.** Ensure `NewsEmptyState()` is shown when the filtered article list, video list, or collection list is empty. Verify the illustration renders correctly.
5. **Stage 5 — polish the interactions.** Add the clear button to the search text field, fix the pill selected colours if needed, and debounce the favourite snackbar.
6. **Stage 6 — verify on device.** Run the app on an Android device or emulator and walk through the full flow: tab switching, filter pills, favourite toggling, search, article open, image gallery open.
7. **Stage 7 — final verification.** Run `flutter analyze` with zero errors in the News feature, run `flutter test`, and check the acceptance checklist.

# 21. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CHECKLIST

## Layout

- The tab bar shows "News" with the search and favourites actions.
- Two main tabs: "News & Reviews" (default) and "Images & Videos".
- When "News & Reviews" is active, filter pills appear: All / Reviews / Special Reports.
- Article cards show cover image, category badge (coloured pill), title (3 lines max), author, time ago, view count.
- Favourite button on each article toggles and shows a snackbar.
- When "Images & Videos" is active, sub-tabs appear: "Images" / "Videos".
- Video cards show cover image, play button, category badge, title, author, time ago, views, likes.
- Collection cards show cover image, 360° badge (if applicable), image count badge, vehicle name.
- Empty state shows the automotive illustration + "All Caught Up" / "You have seen all notifications".
- Skeleton cards appear while data loads (3 vertical blocks).

## Functionality

- Tapping an article opens `ArticleDetailScreen` with the full body text.
- Tapping a video opens `VideoDetailsScreen` with metadata.
- Tapping a collection opens `ImageGalleryScreen` with the image grid.
- Favourite toggle on an article saves/removes it and shows the snackbar.
- Returning from `ArticleDetailScreen` rebuilds the article list with updated favourite icons.
- Search opens `NewsSearchScreen` with a text field; typing filters articles/videos/collections.
- Clear button appears on the search text field when typing.
- Sub-tab switching ("News & Reviews" ↔ "Images & Videos") rebuilds the body correctly.
- The back arrow on every detail screen returns to `NewsScreen`.

## Data integrity

- Every article title and video title matches the mock data.
- Category badge colours are deterministic per the `categoryColorOf()` switch statement.
- View and like counts are positive integers from the mock data.
- Prices (if shown) are in ETB and match the `priceTag` field.
- Favourite state is consistent between the card and the detail screen (when the favourite toggle is implemented there).

## Quality

- `flutter analyze` reports no errors in the News feature (after Stage 1 and Stage 2 fixes).
- `flutter test` passes, including the existing tab navigation tests.
- The feature works with the shared `MockNewsRepository`, without a second database.
- No unrelated feature was modified or broken.
- All remaining limitations (session-only favourites, no error states for empty lists, search query not persisted) are documented in the report.

# 23. FOLDER STRUCTURE RECOMMENDATION

## Recommended Directory Layout for News Feature

```
lib/features/bottom/news/
├── news.dart                       # NewsScreen (tab page) - public API
├── new_impl.dart                   # Internal implementation (primary development file)
│   ├── widgets/                    # Reusable widgets specific to News
│   │   ├── _ArticleCard.dart       # Article card with cover, badge, title, author
│   │   ├── _VideoCard.dart         # Video card with thumbnail, play button
│   │   ├── _CollectionCard.dart    # Collection card with 360° badge
│   │   ├── _FilterPills.dart       # Filter pills (All / Reviews / Special Reports)
│   │   ├── _UnderlineTab.dart      # Underline tab indicator
│   │   ├── _NewsEmptyState.dart    # Empty state illustration + text
│   │   ├── _NewsSkeletonCards.dart # Loading skeleton cards
│   │   ├── _SearchHeaderDelegate.dart # Pinned search header delegate
│   │   ├── _SearchBar.dart         # Search field widget
│   │   ├── _ArticleDetailScreen.dart # Article detail screen
│   │   ├── _VideoDetailsScreen.dart # Video detail screen
│   │   └── _ImageGalleryScreen.dart # Image gallery screen
│   ├── models/                     # Domain models (reuse where possible)
│   │   ├── news_article.dart       # NewsArticle model (shared structure)
│   │   ├── news_video.dart         # NewsVideo model
│   │   └── vehicle_image_collection.dart # VehicleImageCollection model
│   ├── data/                       # Data layer (reuse where possible)
│   │   ├── mock_news_repository.dart # MockNewsRepository (single data source)
│   │   └── favorites_store.dart     # FavoritesStore (in-memory tracking)
│   └── news_cars_page.dart        # The main page widget assembling all sections
├── services/                       # API/services (if needed - none for mock data)
│   └── news_service.dart
└── docs/                           # Local documentation
    └── news_implementation.md

## Key Reuse Patterns (per news.doc)

### 1. News Article Model
- **Reuse**: `lib/features/bottom/news/models/news_article.dart`'s `NewsArticle` model
- **Critical**: Do NOT create a second `NewsArticle` model or second data model
- **Import**: Import `NewsArticle` from the models file, not from any other feature
- **Search**: `NewsArticle.searchMatches()` method for keyword search across title, category, keywords

### 2. News Video Model
- **Reuse**: `lib/features/bottom/news/models/news_video.dart`'s `NewsVideo` model
- **Critical**: Do NOT create a second `NewsVideo` model
- **Structure**: Shares same pattern as NewsArticle (id, title, imageAsset, author, timeAgo, views, body)

### 3. Vehicle Image Collection
- **Reuse**: `lib/features/bottom/news/models/vehicle_image_collection.dart`'s `VehicleImageCollection` model
- **Search**: `VehicleImageCollection.searchMatches()` method
- **Critical**: Do NOT create a second collection model

### 4. Mock News Repository (SINGLE DATA SOURCE)
- **Reuse**: `lib/features/bottom/news/data/mock_news_repository.dart`'s `MockNewsRepository`
- **CRITICAL**: Do NOT create a second repository or second data source
- **Methods**: `fetchArticles()`, `fetchVideos()`, `fetchCollections()`, `searchArticles()`, `searchVideos()`, `searchCollections()`
- **All widgets** must read from `MockNewsRepository` only - no inline data lists

### 5. Favorites Store (SINGLE INSTANCE)
- **Reuse**: `lib/features/bottom/news/data/favorites_store.dart`'s `FavoritesStore.instance`
- **CRITICAL**: Do NOT create a second favorites store
- **Usage**: Both `ArticleDetailScreen` and `_ArticleCard` use `FavoritesStore.instance`
- **Session-scoped**: Documented limitation per section 22 - lost on app restart

### 6. Shared Widgets (DO NOT duplicate)
| Widget | Location | Usage |
|--------|----------|-------|
| `NewsSkeletonCards` | `lib/features/bottom/news/widgets/news_skeleton_cards.dart` | Loading placeholders for articles, videos, collections |
| `NewsEmptyState` | `lib/features/bottom/news/widgets/news_empty_state.dart` | Empty state illustration + text |
| `PageTopBar` | `lib/shared/widgets/page_top_bar.dart` | Top bar with title + trailing actions (shared with Alerts) |
| `NewsArticle` model | `lib/features/bottom/news/models/news_article.dart` | Article structure + categoryColorOf() + searchMatches() |
| `NewsVideo` model | `lib/features/bottom/news/models/news_video.dart` | Video structure |

### 7. Bottom Navigation Integration
- **Reuse**: Existing 5-item bottom nav (New, Used, Compare, **News**, Alerts)
- **News at index 3**: Teal when selected, `AppIcons.news` (`LucideIcons.newspaper`)
- **Do NOT**: Add second navigation bar inside News page
- **Shell ownership**: The navigation shell owns the bottom nav; News tab lives inside PageView

### 8. Color & Theme Integration
- **Reuse**: Existing `app_colors.dart` palette
- **Teal**: `#0F8F83` for selected states, filter pills, category badges
- **Primary**: `#1B5E20` for main color (Ethiopian flag green), section headings
- **Surface**: `#FAFAFA` for card backgrounds
- **Divider**: `#E0E0E0` for dividers, skeletons
- **Text Primary**: `#1A1A2E` for titles, article text
- **Text Secondary**: `#6B6B6B` for metadata, author, time ago
- **Pale teal**: `#EAF7F5` for icon backgrounds (filter pills, category badges)

### 9. Category Colour Mapping
- **Reuse**: `categoryColorOf()` from `news_article.dart`
- **Deterministic**: Each category gets a consistent colour
- **Switch statement**: Reviews, Road Test, Features, Special Reports, EV News, New Cars, Used Cars, Car Prices, Maintenance, Buying Guide, News/default
- **Critical**: Do NOT duplicate the colour mapping - use the shared `categoryColorOf()` function

### 10. Filter Pills
- **Reuse**: Pill styling and behaviour pattern from news.dart
- **Options**: All / Reviews / Special Reports
- **Selected**: Teal text with teal underline, unselected: dark gray
- **Do NOT**: Create duplicate filter pill implementations

### 11. Sub-tabs (News & Reviews vs Images & Videos)
- **Reuse**: Tab switching pattern from news.dart
- **Two main tabs**: "News & Reviews" (default) and "Images & Videos"
- **Do NOT**: Create separate data fetching for each sub-tab - both display the same data filtered differently

### 12. Error & Empty States
- **Reuse**: `NewsSkeletonCards()` for loading, `NewsEmptyState()` for empty
- **Critical**: Ensure `NewsEmptyState()` is shown when filtered lists are empty (P1-2)
- **Do NOT**: Implement custom error states - use the shared widgets

## Implementation Principles

| Principle | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Single NewsArticle Model** | Only one `NewsArticle` model from `news_article.dart` - never create a second |
| **Single NewsVideo Model** | Only one `NewsVideo` model from `news_video.dart` - never create a second |
| **Single MockRepository** | Only one `MockNewsRepository` - the sole data source; no second repository |
| **Single FavoritesStore** | Only `FavoritesStore.instance` - no second store |
| **Heavy Widget Reuse** | `NewsSkeletonCards`, `NewsEmptyState`, `PageTopBar` are shared - do NOT copy |
| **Incremental Fixes** | Fix P0 issues first (icon constants, const fields) before feature enhancements |
| **ETB Pricing** | All prices in Ethiopian Birr, no INR/lakh notation (per mock data) |
| **Category Colours** | Use shared `categoryColorOf()` - do not duplicate the switch statement |
| **Bottom Nav Single** | 5-item nav only, News at index 3, no second navigation bar |

## Development Workflow

1. **Start with compilation**: Fix P0 issues first (missing AppIcons constants, const field changes)
2. **Fix data wiring**: Ensure all widgets read from `MockNewsRepository`, not inline data
3. **Fix favourite rebuild**: Remove `ListenableBuilder` over-rebuild per P1-1
4. **Wire search screen**: Add query passing through navigator, add clear button
5. **Harden empty states**: Ensure `NewsEmptyState()` shows for empty article/video/collection lists
6. **Polish interactions**: Add clear button to search, fix pill colours, debounce snackbar
7. **Verify on device**: Walk through full flow: tab switching, filter pills, favourite toggling, search

## What NOT to Do

❌ **Do NOT create a second `NewsArticle` model** - import from `news_article.dart` only
❌ **Do NOT create a second `NewsVideo` model** - import from `news_video.dart` only
❌ **Do NOT create a second `MockNewsRepository`** - this is the single data source
❌ **Do NOT create a second favorites store** - use `FavoritesStore.instance` only
❌ **Do NOT duplicate shared widgets** - `NewsSkeletonCards`, `NewsEmptyState`, `PageTopBar` are shared
❌ **Do NOT duplicate category colour mapping** - use shared `categoryColorOf()` function
❌ **Do NOT add a second bottom navigation bar** - the shell owns the bottom nav
❌ **Do NOT invent data** - all data must come from `MockNewsRepository`
❌ **Do NOT claim integrations work unless verified** - document limitations (session-only favorites, no error states for real backends)

⚠️ **Critical**: The News feature must not create a second NewsArticle model, second NewsVideo model, second MockNewsRepository, or second FavoritesStore. These are the top defects blocking correct data flow and state management.

This section serves as a guide for the development team to organize code consistently with the project's existing patterns and the `news.doc` specification, emphasizing the single-model and single-repository constraints that are fundamental to this feature's architecture.

# 22. DEFINITION OF DONE

The News feature is ready when it compiles cleanly, the tab switching and filter pills work, article/video/collection cards render correctly, favourite toggling works with snackbar feedback, the search screen navigates correctly, empty states are shown when appropriate, the layout has been checked on an Android device or emulator, and every remaining limitation is documented.

The implementation report must list:

- Files inspected.
- Files modified or created.
- Code preserved.
- Bugs fixed, including the P0 and P1 items from section 18.
- Redundant code removed and why.
- `flutter analyze` and `flutter test` results, with pre-existing errors listed separately.
- Missing integrations and remaining issues.

Do not claim completion until the implementation and verification have actually been performed.

This is the consolidated master specification for the News feature. Use it as the source of truth, then implement it one stage at a time in OpenCode.